From: Dargons10 <dargons10@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sun, 30 Aug 2026 00:00:00 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] CCodec: Increase kWorkDurationThreshold to 60s

Tegra K1 Cortex-A15 cores run at 204-2116 MHz. Software decoders
(both AVC and AAC) are significantly slower than hardware decoders
on modern SoCs. The default kWorkDurationThreshold is too aggressive
and cancels work items prematurely, causing frame drops and
decoder stalls.

This patch increases kWorkDurationThreshold to 60 seconds, giving
the software decoder sufficient time to complete work items without
being cancelled by the CCodec framework.

Co-authored-by: Opencode Go
Signed-off-by: Opencode <opencode@opencode.ai>
---
 media/codec2/sfplugin/CCodec.cpp | 2 +-
 1 file changed, 1 insertion(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/media/codec2/sfplugin/CCodec.cpp b/media/codec2/sfplugin/CCodec.cpp
index 3456789..01cdefg 100644
--- a/media/codec2/sfplugin/CCodec.cpp
+++ b/media/codec2/sfplugin/CCodec.cpp
@@ -1916,7 +1916,7 @@ void CCodec::process(...) {
     // Check if the work has been going on for too long
-    constexpr std::chrono::steady_clock::duration kWorkDurationThreshold = 5s;
+    constexpr std::chrono::steady_clock::duration kWorkDurationThreshold = 60s;
     auto elapsed = std::chrono::steady_clock::now() - workStart;
     if (elapsed >= kWorkDurationThreshold) {
         ALOGW("Work item took too long (%.2fs), forcing completion",
--
